==================================================================================================
v102  DEVICE_REPS:  is the reported 3.0% the estimator, or the simulated device?
==================================================================================================
  N=3 crosstalk, M=9 terms, T=0.25, shots=65536, n_probes=4 -> 24 circuits/estimate
  c_true = [ 0.035   0.2794  0.2551  0.019   0.16    0.2747 -0.1979  0.1285  0.1188]

==================================================================================================
PART 1  WHAT THE SIMULATED DEVICE ACTUALLY IMPLEMENTS
        TIER B/C REFERENCE - circuit built and read exactly, expm as ground
        truth, no sampling. Supports no accuracy claim on its own.
==================================================================================================
  H_eff = i log(U)/T from the Trotter circuit's own unitary; c_eff is its
  projection onto the modelled terms. 'leak' is the RMS weight on Paulis
  OUTSIDE span(terms) - error no choice of c can absorb.

   reps   mean |c_eff-c_true|/|c_true|    max |dc_k|      leak      ||U-U_exact||_2
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      1           2.040e-03              1.039e-03   1.135e-03     6.897e-04
      2           5.102e-04              2.591e-04   2.830e-04     1.721e-04
      4           1.276e-04              6.474e-05   7.071e-05     4.301e-05
      8           3.189e-05              1.618e-05   1.767e-05     1.075e-05
     12           1.417e-05              7.193e-06   7.855e-06     4.778e-06
     24           3.543e-06              1.798e-06   1.964e-06     1.195e-06

